; allocator_size_at_the_maximum: a size exactly at the maximum allocator
; size succeeds on both implementations, under a budget large enough that
; the charge is not what decides it.
;
; Paired with allocator_size_past_the_maximum, which pins the same
; boundary's rejecting side; together they pin the boundary itself rather
; than only the rejection. spec/xqvm/SPEC.md's "Allocator validation
; order" (Allocation budget section, QUI-1315) resolves an allocator's
; size operand as: reject a negative size, charge the budget for it,
; reject a size past MAX_ALLOCATION_SIZE = 2^32 - 1 = 4294967295, and only
; then narrow it to the target's native width -- infallible once step 3
; has passed. size = 4294967295 is exactly the maximum, so step 3 admits
; it and BQMX allocates.
;
; size = 4294967295 costs size * 8 = 34359738360 bytes to charge, just
; under 32 GiB. The vector's budget is set to 68719476736 bytes (64 GiB),
; the same as its sibling vector, so the charge at step 2 succeeds well
; before step 3 is reached. BQMX allocates a sparse model
; (XqmxModel::new stores size as a number and materialises no buffer), so
; this budget costs no real memory despite the size.

PUSH 4294967295
BQMX r0
HALT
